// Per-node-kind iconography — glossy, dimensional illustrations in the classic
// "Cobalt Strike / Havoc session-graph" idiom, so an operator reads a node's TYPE
// from a rich, instantly-recognizable image even at the 52px map node size. Each
// icon is a small SVG scene drawn in a 0 0 64 64 viewBox: metallic bezels, bright
// glass screens with sheen + glow, bold OS logos, drive bays, status LEDs and a soft
// contact shadow.
//
// Color is INTRINSIC to the icon (brand colors for OS logos, blue domain globes,
// gold certificates...). COMPROMISE is signalled separately by the node's red border
// ring + warmed chip fill (see viz.ts / NetworkMap), so the icon itself stays
// full-color and legible whether a node is clean or owned.
//
// Every icon shares one PALETTE of gradients, inlined into each data: URI by
// iconDataUri (each icon is its own document, so the fixed gradient ids never
// collide). Each kind ships a RECOMMENDED default (`ICONS`) plus alternate
// form-factor variants (`ICON_VARIANTS` — e.g. monitor / laptop / all-in-one for a
// Windows host, switch / router / firewall for a network device). Operators pick a
// variant per kind via the campaign theme (`theme.variants`), and may also remap
// which kind's icon a kind uses (`theme.glyphs` / `glyphKey`).
//
// This file is generated by the icon-redesign render lab; hand-edits are fine but
// keep each scene legible at 52px and never bake compromise state into the art.

